## Migration Analysis

Your code has **three** patterns that break on .NET 8:

| API | Problem on .NET 8 |
|-----|-------------------|
| `Thread.Abort()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` |
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Obsolete (`SYSLIB0046` in .NET 9), unreliable for waking `WaitOne` |
| `ManualResetEvent.WaitOne()` without cancellation | Can't be cooperatively cancelled |

Additionally, there's a **race condition** in the original: multiple `Enqueue` calls can signal `_newEvent` but `Reset()` clears it after processing only one item, losing events.

---

## Migrated Code (.NET 8)

```csharp
using System.Threading.Channels;

public class EventProcessor : IDisposable
{
    private readonly Channel<string> _channel = Channel.CreateUnbounded<string>();
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _cts = new();
    private Task? _processingTask;

    public void Start()
    {
        _processingTask = Task.Run(() => RunLoopAsync(_cts.Token));
    }

    private async Task RunLoopAsync(CancellationToken token)
    {
        try
        {
            await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(token))
            {
                Handle(item);
            }
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException) when (token.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            // Normal shutdown — nothing to do.
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        _channel.Writer.TryWrite(item);
    }

    public async Task StopAsync()
    {
        _channel.Writer.Complete();      // Signal no more items
        _cts.CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5)); // Timeout fallback
        if (_processingTask is not null)
            await _processingTask;
    }

    private void Handle(string item)
    {
        // Your processing logic here
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        _cts.Dispose();
    }
}
```

